      "content": "If a sensor flags a temperature excursion during customs delays, onsite teams must immediately isolate the samples and physically separate any unaffected units to prevent cross-contamination. They should activate the emergency backup cooling mechanism while documenting the exact time, location, and environmental conditions for a post-incident analysis. Depending on the duration and severity confirmed by the asset manager, the shipment must either be rebooted with verified refrigerants or diverted to a secure quarantine facility for potential re-testing at a recognized lab before redistribution.",
